# Pilot read and error cases (PILOTS_ENABLED=1 on both sides). Each backend
# runs against its own copy of the scratch DB, seeded identically:
#   docker exec norviq-v2-schema-pg createdb -U pg parity_pilots_a (and _b), then
#   pg_dump -U pg norviq | psql -U pg parity_pilots_X   (inside the container)
#   psql .../parity_pilots_a -f parity/pilots-setup.sql; same for _b
#   Vapor (own instance, killed within 200 s: its ingestion job fires at 240 s):
#     DATABASE_NAME=parity_pilots_a JWT_SECRET=parity-secret PILOTS_ENABLED=1 StockPlanBackend serve --port 18148
#   v2: DATABASE_NAME=parity_pilots_b PILOTS_ENABLED=1 PORT=18147 go run ./cmd/api serve
#   go run ./cmd/parity -a http://127.0.0.1:18148 -b http://127.0.0.1:18147 -jwt-secret parity-secret -cases parity/pilots.jsonl
# Then parity/pilots-writes.jsonl (needs a freshly seeded pair of copies).
